<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/05c0229d4372> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver states the vehicle was in Autopilot mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1537" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/074e5db41da3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1538] On its website, Tesla explains that although the autopilot has steering and braking capabilities, it does not make the vehicle autonomous and is only meant to be used when the driver is 'fully attentive' and prepared to take the wheel at any time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1538" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b23753f3cee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1793] Tesla Inc. warns drivers that the system is not fully autonomous and that drivers who use it must be ready to intervene." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e1e82ceec81> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1793] A government report says the driver of a Tesla sedan that slammed into a Culver City firetruck on the 405 Freeway last year was using the car’s Autopilot system" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/12e0b429a16d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1538] The National Highway Police Bureau (NHPB) said the driver of the Tesla was a 53-year-old man surnamed Huang (黃), who claimed that he had set the car to run on autopilot" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1538" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/195594e78fa7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla declined to comment on that." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1537" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c1819c5d500> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1792] What makes the story newsworthy is that the Culver City Firefighters Local 1927 tweeted that the driver of the Tesla Model S reported that the luxury electric car was traveling in Autopilot mode when it struck the un-moving huge, red firetruck." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1792" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/22773c835eca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1538] On its website, Tesla explains that although the autopilot has steering and braking capabilities, it does not make the vehicle autonomous and is only meant to be used when the driver is 'fully attentive' and prepared to take the wheel at any time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1538" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/33ec3e7e8d99> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1794] The results of the NTSB's investigation of the crash involved a Tesla Model S P85 and a Culver City Fire Department Culver City Engine 42 in the high-occupancy vehicle lane of southbound Interstate 405." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1794" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4d48269d8674> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Why does Tesla autopilot not perceive such a large obstacle on the road as this, with its use of cameras and radar?" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1537" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/55f806ebd091> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1794] A driver's inattention, overreliance on his car's advanced driver assistance system, and use of the system inconsistent with manufacturer guidance, coupled with the system permitting driver disengagement from the driving task, led to the Jan. 22, 2018, crash" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1794" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6071fc0f3dd6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NTSB Issues Report on Tesla Crash with Culver City Fire Engine" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1794" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/630f8a126842> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1538] On its website, Tesla explains that although the autopilot has steering and braking capabilities, it does not make the vehicle autonomous and is only meant to be used when the driver is 'fully attentive' and prepared to take the wheel at any time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1538" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/65656e75d41d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1793] Tesla Inc. warns drivers that the system is not fully autonomous and that drivers who use it must be ready to intervene." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1793" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/658f7b2ff64a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla In Taiwan Crashes Directly Into Overturned Truck, Ignores Pedestrian, With Autopilot On" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1537" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c277298434a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1538] On its website, Tesla explains that although the autopilot has steering and braking capabilities, it does not make the vehicle autonomous and is only meant to be used when the driver is 'fully attentive' and prepared to take the wheel at any time." ;
